  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04TI">Definition <span data-tag="04TI">94.16.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack over $S$. A <em>presentation</em> of $\mathcal{X}$ is given by a smooth groupoid $(U, R, s, t, c)$ in algebraic spaces over $S$, and an equivalence $f : [U/R] \to \mathcal{X}$. </p>
